From b96257abe493e2672c8f298a8627565832f0e55c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): share bounded native UI programs and resource
 conversion

Provide immutable JSON UI declarations, scoped expression evaluation, domain bindings and bounded scene contracts before packet integration. Keep accepted pack layering, textures, fonts and builtin UI identity in one resource lifecycle.

The following transport patch registers form, NPC, HUD and container presentation without changing these APIs. Tests for the evaluator, bindings, texture limits and message codecs live with this prerequisite.

Resolve descendant declarations such as main_screen_content/server_form_factory
in the owning template and instance scopes. Preserve those declarations across
program export, retain inline properties when an explicit parent changes, and
resolve relative children in the replacement namespace. The pinned executable
control visitor confirms slash-separated paths with template suffixes removed;
full definition-store merge precedence remains inferred from versioned inputs.

Accept bounded relative texture paths containing a tilde. The Enchanted pack
uses these filenames; share validation between loading and scene resolution
so accepted pixels and metadata survive conversion.

Honor bound local collection counts and control-ID lists without requiring a
server controller to own their generated rows. Separate generated indices
from controller scopes, preserve sparse list indices, and leave rows beyond
controller data without response actions. Keep unknown uncounted collections
as errors and retain scene limits.

Original pinned-client property-dispatch fixtures verify integer/list count
updates, while expression fixtures show boolean arithmetic retaining an
integer result. Preserve that type so authored count predicates activate
rather than becoming ignored real-valued updates. These fixtures do not
execute the complete native child factory or renderer lifecycle.

Only locally bound properties override a control's authored rendered fields.
Keep panel texture values available to binding expressions without treating
them as panel images. The captured Enchanted advertisement and kits forms
now resolve authored scenes with their original visible response indices.
A missing progress template and live visual parity remain unverified.

Add the pinned brewing-stand screen to the shared container program with
its three indexed bottle cells and fixed ingredient/fuel collections.
Keep all 41 actual Java slot addresses, count annotations and inventory
actions. Bind the native empty-cell placeholders to actual stack counts.
Publish bound image clip ratios so all three native progress images use
their controller values instead of remaining fully drawn.

Port the target 1.26.51.1 brewing UI callback arithmetic. A private probe
executes complete callbacks 146c8a310, 146c8a350 and 146c8a440 plus helpers
14c53cd40, 14c53cbc0 and 14c53cf70. All 994 counter cases match the Java
float bits, including the full brew cycle, large int32 values and partial
fuel updates with a zero total. Two missing-actor/type controls return
empty indicators. The fixture supplies initialized models, reference
objects, CFG, world/chunk/actor lookup and the virtual type predicate;
actor construction, controller input and GPU parity are not claimed.

Negotiate workstation programs on format 4 and retain full signed int32
counter snapshots under the same menu ID and presentation sequence.
Existing formats reject the new family before writing any bytes. A
separate bounded counter codec permits live updates without inventory
snapshots or a second item authority. Export/import and actual bundled
scene tests retain fixed slot actions, indexed bottles and live clipping.

Add the shared furnace, blast-furnace and smoker program model, ordered
recipe books, bounded preview snapshots and exact revision identities for
activation and recipe requests. Keep recipe renderer references distinct
from real Java slot references. Generalize singleton collections so cooking
and brewing use the same fixed-slot binding path.

Load overrides for the pinned native ui_defs declarations without a pack
repeating that list or scanning arbitrary UI files. Resolve screen content
as a required definition so missing defaults cannot become empty panels.

Port the target cooking tab and layout transitions. Fresh executable probes
verify 2,700 tab queries, 140 tab callbacks, 64 layout callbacks and 176 flame
arithmetic cases, including two native division traps. Native query/model,
allocation and downstream setter seams are supplied as documented in the
private fixtures. These do not establish full controller or GPU parity.

The shared cooking contracts are a prerequisite for the authoritative
catalog and client producer. This patch does not advertise cooking screens
or replace ordinary workstation controls by itself. Targeted model, codec,
progress, navigation and existing container tests pass all 61 cases.

Transport raw cooking progress independently of item authority. Frequent
actor-property updates must not replace a recipe/inventory snapshot or
restart activation. Bind progress to its exact menu, presentation and
item update, and retain the monotonic native data revision. Preserve all
four signed int32 properties without Java furnace normalization.

Validate cooking recipe action paths independently of unrelated controls.
A live cooking model exposes an unresolved enabled binding on its search
textbox; that control cannot dispatch recipes and must not invalidate
otherwise bound recipe actions. Collect the owning paths first and keep
strict visibility/enabled validation on all recipe controls and ancestors.
A hidden owner does not require an enabled value. Do not invent a search
controller value or relax unknown states on any active action path.

Preserve the authored primary, secondary and tertiary recipe command in
the action envelope. Version three rejects older envelopes because their
missing input mode cannot safely default to Java placement semantics.
Echo the mode in the exact request identity and reject unknown mode bytes;
this contract does not establish native quantity or cursor behavior.

Preserve native cooking event phases 0, 1, and 2 separately from input
commands and transfer quantities. The original state dispatcher uses phase 0
for initial primary selection and phase 2 for selected-state release.
Action and result envelopes use version 5 so earlier inputs cannot silently
gain a default controller mode or phase. Physical input mapping and the
complete authored cooking action backend remain separate unfinished work.

Bind authored recipe authority to the exact sorted, visible collection cell,
not only membership in the visible recipe set. Reject a missing or malformed
collection index and an ID from another visible cell. Preserve integer JSON
identity instead of coercing real indices such as 7.0. Native 1.26.51.1 event
callbacks retain typed collection indices and resolve recipe_book through
the active tab; the separate slot resolver differs on the inventory tab.

Two behavioral regressions fail before this validation change. Additional
private fixtures execute 240 original event-source controls and six genuine
selection/release steps with the native cooking manager and input graph.
Recipe data and external game interfaces remain controlled; full cooking
controller ownership, placement, repeated selection, wire requests, and
live acceptance remain unverified.

Publish the pinned cooking controller's seven tab and layout constants.
Original publisher146c44040 supplies food/items/blocks/search/inventory
indices 1..5 and survival/recipe-book layouts 1/2. Without these globals,
authored grouped toggles resolve without their forced selection indices.
The bundled-scene regression retains the indices across export/import for
all three cooking families and fails before this change. This restores
control identity; complete input handlers and visual parity remain open.

Export cooking programs from the same MenuView as their snapshot. Include
the live tab label in translation dependency discovery alongside the
authoritative title. Controller labels can change after native tab and
filter updates without appearing as literals in the authored UI closure.
Omitting them left localized search captions as raw keys on the client.

A full-scene and action-scope round trip over all three cooking families
preserves accepted-pack translations. Removing the live label dependency
fails the regression; restoring it passes. Native caption source keys,
text callbacks, input mapping and complete screen parity remain separate
verification requirements.

Use the pinned146c94ae0 tab-label getter rules in shared navigation. Search
uses the all-recipes key while filtering is disabled and family-specific
keys while enabled. The inventory tab uses craftingScreen.tab.survival.
Sixty complete native getter controls bind these branches with explicit
allocator/CRT boundaries and ingredient descriptor identities. Restoring
either earlier rule independently fails the native comparison.

Transport the native controller input mode separately from the recipe
command and phase. All four verified numeric modes remain distinct, and
unknown modes or earlier payload versions reject. The active-device mode
getter and focused recipe path have separate native references; this
context field does not assert a physical device mapping. The Fabric mouse
adapter sends its explicit mouse context instead of inferring mode two.

Publish reusable cooking search and text-coalescing APIs before connecting
the menu transport. Preserve raw pending text until a ready tick, apply
only the latest edit, and retain both applied and pending text when the
native guarded mode-two clear declines the event. Model-clear and settings
effects remain the integrating caller's responsibility.

Search uses the target's Unicode 5.0 compatibility composition and full
case folding. Repackage the checksum-pinned public utf8proc 1.1.5 tables
with their MIT and Unicode notices; do not substitute a modern Unicode
library. Invalid UTF-8 preserves the whole input, while valid results end
at NUL. Match normalized primary names first, then normalized secondary
labels after the native byte-formatting automaton. Keep name producers
lazy and supplied by the caller, rather than using Java preview names.

Native fixtures and full-codepoint public comparisons verify these shared
primitives. Production name/label acquisition, repeated native eligibility
checks, exact menu ownership, transport, physical edit admission and the
actual search widget remain required integration work. These APIs do not
make the unfinished default cooking screen actionable.

Share native unfiltered primary-name selection and custom-name dispatch.
Preserve empty and wrongly typed custom-name presence, and use a written
book title when its display name is empty. Keep filtered names separate.
Apply ordinary appended group/body/custom text with typed-byte admission
and preserve the native color-argument order. Definition-owned ordinary
names and language lookup remain caller responsibilities.

Fresh original-executable controls cover 1,299 base/component/coal/append
cases and 1,000 custom/book cases. The shared selector matches all 2,286
applicable selection/append rows. Key dispatch controls remain separate.
Three deliberate name-selection regressions fail assertion checks. These
controls do not establish full registry, localization, screen or GPU parity.

Resolve complete authored cooking screen hosts through the shared control
expander instead of selecting only their content panel. Preserve screen
input mappings, profile variables, policies, overlays and inherited control
hierarchy in direct and transported scenes. Require an actual screen root;
independent authored screens must declare their own content graph.
The pinned default Furnace, Blast Furnace and Smoker hosts resolve with no
missing templates and round-trip exactly through program export. Existing
slot/recipe authority, titles, layering and payload bounds remain enforced.
This preserves the authored contract; unsupported client controller and
screen-policy behavior still requires implementation and admission checks.

Finalize UI inheritance in declaration load order. Fill absent members from
non-null ancestor fields, retain explicit local nulls, and reuse completed
parents. Stop at missing or visited ancestors, including native self
references, without weakening recursive control expansion bounds. Apply
array modifications to a fresh finalized template. Preserve declaration
order in exported closures so transported programs resolve identically.
Use the same finalizer for accepted declarations and native HUD baselines.

Original 1.26.51.1 registry constructor 1403f3f20, finalizer 14043efd0 and
lookup 1403f69f0 confirm these semantics. Typed loader-output records cover
250 three-node parent graphs and the exact furnace_pocket self declaration.
All 751 lookups match Java directly and after export, 1,502 comparisons.
The capture stops at 140440ed0 before external scheduling and cleanup;
it does not establish resource-loader ordering, complete native screen
construction, physical input, pixels or full lifecycle parity.

Share recipe collection partitioning between cooking and grouped player
recipes. Preserve stable four-state buckets, contiguous catalog identity,
first-member representatives, and icon/count-based expansion history.
Ungrouped filtering retains its existing visible-prefix semantics.

Original 1.26.51.1 routines 143445150, 143446b90, 143447710 and 143447ab0
provide 4,128 collection cases and ten retained-state steps. Six additional
steps distinguish catalog identity from icon/count header identity. Item
copying, icon comparison, availability evaluation and external callbacks
remain supplied boundaries. Recipe acquisition, full player controller,
physical input and screen parity remain separate integration work.

Query recipe-row availability independently of refresh so presentation can
observe current evaluator state without replacing its retained snapshot.
Flat rows disable states two and three; grouped rows disable state two,
except for headers matching a retained representative by icon and count.
Member rows do not receive that exemption. Keep the evaluator and native
item comparison explicit at the integration boundary.

Original getter 1434461c0 supplies 3,584 cases with fresh evaluator results
after construction. Three regressions retain snapshot identity, current
availability and header/member distinctions. Full catalog acquisition,
controller ownership, action admission, input and pixels remain unfinished.

Generalize cooking search into NativeRecipeSearch with explicit cooking and
player policies. Player names remove formatting on both branches. Its word
policy requires the full literal query plus any query-token/name-token prefix
match, using ASCII spaces and getline's omitted trailing empty token. Keep
Unicode normalization, raw query bytes and lazy name acquisition shared.
Do not reuse Java preview labels or assume that an ability predicate means
creative mode. Recipe unlock/count inputs and installed player-screen search
remain separate integration work.

Complete original player search 143438780 and word matcher 143438da0 match
1,136 search cases and 1,220 normalized word controls in the pinned
1.26.51.1 build51061372 executable. These controls supply name, unlock,
game-type and standard-stream interfaces. Native formatting, normalization,
validity, matching, vector allocation and cleanup execute. They do not prove
production name acquisition, the full availability evaluator or pixels.

Share the pinned STL sort through NativeSort so cooking priorities and native
ingredient groups retain the same comparator-equivalent ordering. Accept a
comparator directly instead of encoding multiple keys into a synthetic priority.
Keep the Microsoft STL license with the extracted algorithm. Existing cooking
order controls pass; ingredient cardinality/quantity order is checked against
complete original counter executions in the consuming recipe patch.

Convert native bitmap atlases alongside shared UI fonts. Bedrock 1.26.60.5
selects a 449-entry extended map or its 256-entry legacy map. Retain each
atlas's same-pack layout metadata so upper legacy textures cannot inherit
vanilla's new height or mapping. Crop incomplete rows and pad cells only
when Java's ascent constraint requires it, preserving glyph pixel scale.

Resolve Unicode fallback pages in the same ordered layers and export them
after ASCII providers. Keep the final BMP page and advance the conversion
cache revision. Matching executable tables, atlas files, and the official
26.60 changelog establish the input contract. Full native visual comparison
remains pending.

Admit bitmap images, layout metadata, and TrueType files through the
built-in resource boundary so licensed providers reach the converter.
Small Unicode pages retain their pixels with cell padding where Java's
ascent constraint exceeds the original height.

Leave U+0020 to the existing Java space provider in both ASCII and Unicode
output. Java 26.3 gives an empty bitmap cell a one-unit advance, so importing
the blank atlas space would narrow text across menus and chat.

Read image dimensions before decoding and bound padded atlas dimensions
before allocation. Include bitmap pages in the font file budget without
displacing valid TrueType families or the final Unicode pages.
